{"id":29416,"title":"Multivariate volume rendering","url":"https://www.osti.gov/biblio/495676","final_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/495676","year":1996,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"9d4d8f0137fd61e2af37fabe338607f9e6599c68d85d1216111b2f5aa20dbde8","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793063412.1243591,"text_chars":26876,"abstract":"This paper presents a new technique for representing multivalued data sets defined on an integer lattice. It extends the state-of-the-art in volume rendering to include nonhomogeneous volume representations. That is, volume rendering of materials with very fine detail (e.g. translucent granite) within a voxel. Multivariate volume rendering is achieved by introducing controlled amounts of noise within the volume representation. Varying the local amount of noise within the volume is used to represent a separate scalar variable. The technique can also be used in image synthesis to create more realistic clouds and fog.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/495676","https://www.osti.gov/biblio/495676","https://core.ac.uk/download/71170754.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/m2/1/high_res_d/495676.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=volume splatting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=mri volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=direct volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=3d texture based volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=vector field volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=gaussian splatting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=point rendering voxels","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc687575/?q=footpr